# PR-A0: deterministic compliance artifacts.
#
# These files' BYTES are the product: generators write them, CI regenerates
# them and fails on any diff, and later licensing work (THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES,
# vendored licence texts) will extend the same guarantee. Line-ending
# translation on checkout would make the working tree disagree with both the
# repository and a fresh clone — the exact non-determinism the architecture
# review measured (693 of 977 tracked files differing under autocrlf).
#
# Deliberately narrow: only the compliance surface is pinned. This is not a
# repository-wide normalization; a giant line-ending diff is churn, not
# determinism.

LICENSE                  text eol=lf
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt  text eol=lf
compliance/**            text eol=lf
sbom.cdx.json            text eol=lf
MANIFEST.in              text eol=lf

# PR-A2a: corresponding-source archives are BINARY bytes. Without this
# override the compliance/** rule above would let git treat the .tar.gz
# files as text and normalize byte sequences that merely look like line
# endings — corrupting the archives and their recorded hashes.
compliance/third-party-source/*.tar.gz  binary
